# mirror-sync pairs: source|destination, one per line, # comments allowed.
# Copy to mirrors.conf (gitignored) and list your own pairs.
# The destination becomes an EXACT mirror of the source on every run
# (rsync -a --delete): extra files in the destination are deleted.
# Paths are literal; write them out in full (no ~ or $HOME).

# Pairs run one at a time, in this order. The local-drive pairs come first:
# /Volumes/local/Backup is itself a source below, so Documents and
# Protected.dmg reach iCloud on the same night they reach the drive.
# tests/test_mirror_sync.py (PairOrder) fails on a pair listed too late.

# Local Documents. This remains an exact mirror, not a historical archive.
/Users/example/Documents|/Volumes/local/Backup/Documents

# Encrypted archive file, copied into its dedicated destination directory.
/Users/example/Protected.dmg|/Volumes/local/Backup/Protected

# Local folders mirrored into their corresponding iCloud Backup folders.
# The local volume is authoritative, and each pair scopes --delete separately.
/Volumes/local/Photos|/Users/example/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Backup/Photos
/Volumes/local/Backup|/Users/example/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Backup/Backup
